  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Menton and Roquebrune-Cap-Martin, neighbours on the Italian border, form a compact area where you can stay in the centre or towards Garavan and reach the few beaches open to dogs on foot or by car. This page gathers useful pointers before booking; each hotel has its own listing, with its own rule.</p>

      <h2>The area's hotels on Coco Explore</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/en/fiche-hotel-mediterranee-menton">Best Western Hôtel Méditerranée</a>, Menton</li>
        <li><a href="/fiche-hebergement-hotel-menton-riviera-menton">Hôtel Menton Riviera</a> (French page)</li>
        <li><a href="/fiche-hebergement-hotel-royal-westminster-menton">Hôtel Royal Westminster</a> (dogs under 8 kg; French page)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>Beach rules are strict in Menton. The 2023 municipal order reserves two beaches for people accompanied by dogs, all year round, and declares all other beaches prohibited to dogs, even on a leash; swimming for dogs is also prohibited on the concession beaches. In its reminder of 29 April 2026, the town names three set-up beaches: Gorbio beach (boundary with Roquebrune-Cap-Martin), Casino beach and Hawaï beach (Garavan), and announces fines after a week of prevention. The tourist office also mentions a "plage des Chiens" on the promenade Reine-Astrid, with showers, without lifeguard supervision.</p>
      <p>In Roquebrune-Cap-Martin, the tourist office describes the Plage de la Piscine (promenade Robert Schuman, towards the edge of the town in the direction of Menton) as "specially for dogs", free and open all year in 2026. However, the municipal parks and gardens regulations do not admit animals in parks and lawns, even on a leash.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the list of authorised beaches differs slightly between the town's and the tourist office's documents; before laying down your towel, look at the signs and the sails marking out the zones.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Menton also has two fenced dog parks, avenue Blasco Ibanez and corniche Serres de la Madone (see <a href="/en/fiche-activite-parcs-canins-menton">Menton's dog parks</a>), and the <a href="/fiche-plage-casino-menton">Casino beach</a> (French page) has its own listing.</p>
